  "dom_id": "step-q171849",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x<4$\n\nGiven that the above predicate is defined over the universal set $Z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The truth set of $P(x)$ is $∅.$\n\nII. The truth set of $P(x)$ is $Z.$\n\nIII. $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x).$",
  "worked_solution": "The *existential quantification* of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $U,$ transforms this predicate into a statement that we write as\n\n$$\n∃x\\in U,\\,P(x).\n$$\n\nThis statement is true if the predicate $P(x)$ is true for a single element $x\\in U,$ i.e. if the truth set ${T}_{P}$ of the predicate is not empty:\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}\\ne ∅\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the truth set of our predicate is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\{…,1,2,3\\}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The truth set is *not* empty.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, ${T}_{P}\\ne Z.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${T}_{P}$ is not empty, the statement $∃x\\in Z,\\,P(x)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
